e>Davidson</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Powers</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Hedayat</surname><given-names>KM</given-names></name><name><surname>Tieszen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kon</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Shepard</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Spuhler</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Todres</surname><given-names>ID</given-names></name><name><surname>Levy</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Barr</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghandi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirsch</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Armstrong</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Clinical practice guidelines for support of the family in the patient-centered intensive care unit: American College of Critical Care Medicine Task Force 2004&#x02013;2005</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>2007</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>605</fpage><lpage>622</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17205007</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.CCM.0000254067.14607.EB</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Corr</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A task-based approach to coping with dying</article-title><source>Omega: Journal of Death and Dying</source><year>1992</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>81</fpage><lpage>94</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sloan</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name><name><surname>Bagiella</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Powell</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Religion, spirituality, and medicine</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>1999</year><volume>353</volume><fpage>664</fpage><lpage>667</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10030348</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0140-6736(98)07376-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Levin JS</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Investigating the epidemiologic effects of religious experience: findings. explanations and barriers</article-title><source>Religion in aging and health: theoretical foundations and methodological frontiers</source><year>1994</year><publisher-name>Thousand Oaks, Calif.; London: Sage Publications</publisher-name><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>17</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>PC</given-names></name><name><surname>Pargament</surname><given-names>KI</given-names></name><name><surname>Hood</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name><name><surname>McCullough</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Swyers</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Larson</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Zinnbauer</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Conceptualizing Religion and Spirituality: Points of Commonality, Points of Departure</article-title><source>Journal for the Theory of Social Behaviour</source><year>2000</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>77</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/1468-5914.00119</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>James</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><source>Varieties of Religious Experience</source><year>1902</year><publisher-name>New York: Longmans</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Emerson</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An Address delivered before the Senior Class in Divinity College, Cambridge, Sunday Evening 15 July 1838</article-title><source>Boston Quarterly Review</source><year>1838</year></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hay</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>Exploring Inner Space</source><year>1987</year><publisher-name>Harmondsworth: Penguin</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wach</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Comparative Study of Religions</source><year>1958</year><publisher-name>New York: Columbia University Press</publisher-name><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">13538626</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sheldrake</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><source>Spirituality and History: Questions of Interpretation and Method</source><year>1992</year><publisher-name>New York: Crossroad</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Koenig</surname><given-names>HG</given-names></name><name><surname>McCullough</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Larson</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><source>Handbook of religion and health</source><year>2001</year><publisher-name>Oxford; New York; Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Larson</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Swyers</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>McCullough</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><source>Scientific Research on Spirituality and Health: A Consensus Report</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>Rockville, MD: National Institute for Healthcare Research</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tanyi</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Towards clarification of the meaning of spirituality</article-title><source>J Adv Nurs</source><year>2002</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>500</fpage><lpage>509</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12175360</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2648.2002.02315.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cupitt</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>Mysticism after Modernity</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>England: Blackwell</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>ICM Research Ltd</collab></person-group><article-title>What the world thinks of God</article-title><year>2004</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://news.bbc.co.uk/1/hi/programmes/wtwtgod/3518375.stm"/></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Harris Interactive Inc</collab></person-group><article-title>Harris Poll: The religious and other beliefs of Americans</article-title><year>2003</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http:///www.harrisinteractive.com/harris_poll/index.asp?PID=359"/></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hay</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Morisy</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reports of ecstatic, paranormal or religious experience in Great Britain and the United States: a comparison of trends</article-title><source>Journal for the Scientific Study of Religion</source><year>1978</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>255</fpage><lpage>268</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/1386320</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hay</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Nye</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><source>The Spirit of the Child</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>London: Jessica Kingsley</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Speck</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Royal Free interview for spiritual and religious beliefs: development and validation of a self-report version</article-title><source>Psychol Med</source><year>2001</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>1015</fpage><lpage>1023</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11513369</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S0033291701004160</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>King</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Barnes</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Low</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilkinson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Mason</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Sutherland</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tookman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measuring spiritual belief: development and standardization of a Beliefs and Values Scale</article-title><source>Psychol Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>417</fpage><lpage>425</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16288679</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1017/S003329170500629X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Voas</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Crockett</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Religion in Britain: Neither Believing nor Belonging</article-title><source>Sociology</source><year>2005</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>11</fpage><lpage>28</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/0038038505048998</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Debray</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><source>God: an itinerary</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>London: Verso</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Durkheim</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><source>The elementary forms of the religious life: a study in religious sociology</source><year>1912</year><publisher-name>London: Allen &#x00026; Unwin</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hayes</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Making sense of spirituality</article-title><source>Behaviorism</source><year>1984</year><volume>12</volume><fpage